---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import { toolFamilies, marketplace, installLibrary } from '../data/tools';
---

<Layout
  title="ExFu tools & documentation"
  description="Find the ExFu Agent Library, planning and delegating tools, plan visualiser and humane agents. Source, documentation and setup support."
  ><section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow red">ExFu tools</p><h1>Pick up where<br />you left off.</h1><p
        class="lead tools-lead"
      >
        Find your tools, installation instructions and documentation. If you’re new here, the
        marketplace is the place to explore what’s available.
      </p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/ExFu/exfu-marketplace"
        >Open the marketplace ↗</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="setup" class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="setup-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow red">Installing for the first time?</p><h2>Let’s get you set up.</h2><p>
          The Agent Library is a good starting point for your own work. It gives Claude a place for
          your context, preferences and ongoing tasks. Install it first, then let Claude walk you
          through setting up your library.
        </p><p>
          You’ll need Claude Desktop with Cowork available, or Claude Code already installed and
          signed in. Choose the route you use below.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="setup-options">
        <article class="setup-option">
          <h3>In Cowork</h3><p>Use the buttons in Claude Desktop. No terminal needed.</p><ol>
            <li>Open Cowork, then <strong>Customize → Plugins</strong>.</li><li>
              Under Personal plugins, choose <strong>+ → Add marketplace</strong>, then add from a
              repository. Paste this address:
            </li>
          </ol><CopyBlock text={marketplace} label="Copy marketplace address" /><p>
            Browse the added marketplace and install <strong>exfu-agent-library-solo</strong>.
            That’s the Agent Library for individuals.
          </p><p>
            <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837440-use-plugins-in-claude"
              >Claude’s illustrated plugin guide ↗</a
            >
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="setup-option">
          <h3>In Claude Code</h3><p>
            Open your terminal and run this command. It adds the marketplace and installs the Agent
            Library.
          </p><CopyBlock text={installLibrary} label="Copy Agent Library install command" /><p>
            Already inside a Claude Code conversation? Run these two commands there, one at a time:
          </p><CopyBlock text="/plugin marketplace add ExFu/exfu-marketplace" /><CopyBlock
            text="/plugin install exfu-agent-library-solo@exfu-marketplace"
          /><p>
            <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/discover-plugins"
              >Claude Code plugin instructions ↗</a
            >
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="setup-next" id="first-session">
        <p class="eyebrow red">Once it’s installed</p><h2>Give your library a home.</h2><p>
          Create a folder called <strong>ExFu Library</strong> somewhere you can find it again. Start
          a fresh Claude session with access to that folder. If the plugin hasn’t appeared yet, restart
          Claude first.
        </p><p>Paste this to begin:</p><CopyBlock
          text="I’ve installed the ExFu Agent Library and created an ExFu Library folder. Help me get set up using the ExFu setup skill. Ask me where the folder is, then walk me through it one step at a time."
          label="Copy setup prompt"
        /><p>
          Bring one real task you’d like help with. Claude can ask about your work and preferences,
          help organise the context, and explain what it’s creating. You can add more as you go.
        </p><p>
          Next time, choose the same library folder. Ask for the ExFu guides whenever you want to
          understand the setup or learn what else you can do.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h3>Something not working?</h3><div class="setup-options">
        <article>
          <h4>I can’t find the plugin.</h4><p>
            Check that the ExFu marketplace was added and the Agent Library is installed and
            enabled. Start a new session after installing. On a managed work account, your
            administrator may need to allow it.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h4>Claude doesn’t recognise the setup.</h4><p>
            Check you’re using the app where you installed the plugin and have selected your library
            folder. Ask Claude whether it can see the ExFu setup skill. If it cannot, restart the
            app and check the installed plugins again.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div><p>
        Still stuck? Email <a href="mailto:al@exfu.ai">al@exfu.ai</a> with the app you’re using, the step
        you reached and the error message. Leave out passwords and private client information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section><section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Tools for working with agents.</h2><div class="tool-directory">
        {
          toolFamilies.map((tool, i) => (
            <article>
              <>
                <span class="tool-mark" aria-hidden="true">
                  {['↳', '⇄', '◎', '≋'][i]}
                </span>
                <div>
                  <>
                    <h3>{tool.name}</h3>
                    <p>{tool.description}</p>
                    <p>{tool.detail}</p>
                    <p>Claude Code terminal · after adding the marketplace:</p>
                    <CopyBlock
                      text={`claude plugin install ${tool.pkg}@exfu-marketplace`}
                      label={`Copy ${tool.name} plugin command`}
                    />
                    <a class="text-link" href={marketplace}>
                      Find it in the marketplace ↗
                    </a>
                  </>
                </div>
              </>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div><div class="tools-help">
        <h2>Need a hand with your setup?</h2><p>
          If you’re already using the tools, tell me which one and where you’re getting stuck. If
          you want help setting up agents around your work, personal support may be a useful
          starting point.
        </p><div>
          <a class="button" href="mailto:al@exfu.ai">Ask Alastair ↗</a><a
            class="text-link"
            href="/personal-support/">Explore personal support</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section></Layout
>
